 "relevance_note": "Cohort of 26 patients with inborn errors of immunity including one TNFAIP3 carrier with individual-level data: \"mutations in IL2RG (P19), CTLA4 (P20–P21), TNFAIP3 (P22)\".",
 "method_note": "Hand-extracted; no script transcription of tables. Only P22 (TNFAIP3:c.2152del) is in scope; the other 25 cohort members carry variants in other genes and get no rows (cohort_size_as_stated = 26). CONTRADICTION: P22's sex is 'M' in Table 1 but 'F' in Tables S3 and S4; sex recorded as 'not reported'. Age at last evaluation taken from the Age column of Table S3/S4 ('4Y'), which is the age at immunological testing in this cross-sectional study; it differs from the onset/diagnosis age of 40 months in Table 1. Zygosity 'heterozygous' is from a Discussion sentence about 'One patient harboring a heterozygous mutation in the TNFAIP3 gene'; the cohort has a single TNFAIP3 patient, so the sentence identifies P22. Autoantibodies: routine evaluation negative (recorded as excluded 'positive autoantibodies on routine evaluation'), but antigen microarray showed significantly elevated autoantibodies (recorded observed); checklist 'autoantibodies (ANA/other)' set to observed on the microarray finding. Skin lesions checklist set observed from 'Eczema' in Table 1. Empty Table 1 cells (Infection, Digestive symptom, Lymphoproliferative) and '-' in Tables S1/S2 (symbol undefined) treated as not reported. '#' and '$' markers in Tables S3/S4 are not defined in their legends, so lymphocyte and immunoglobulin values were not interpreted as abnormal. disease_label_as_stated: the paper never names A20 haploinsufficiency or HA20; the only person-level diagnosis given is type 1 diabetes, and the cohort-level diagnosis is IEI. Pathogenicity left 'not reported': 'a spectrum of pathogenic mutations' is a cohort-wide statement. Hyperglycemia was the initial symptom in Table 1; its onset was not assigned the 40-month onset age.",
